#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""orca-desktop-update: updater for this Windows machine's Orca desktop app.

The Windows counterpart of `orca-serve-update --desktop`. It speaks the same JSON
protocol (status / check / prepare / apply / rollback / recover), so orca-fleet
drives a `"local": true` server entry the same way on every platform. It is
installed next to orca-fleet by client/install.sh and needs no administrator
rights: Orca's Windows installer is a per-user NSIS setup
(%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Programs\\orca).

An update quits the app (WM_CLOSE, then a forced kill after
app_stop_timeout_seconds), runs the official installer silently, relaunches the
app through Explorer (a clean, job-free process with the shell's environment)
and verifies the runtime version and process stability, rolling back on
failure. Terminals live in Orca's PTY daemon, which runs from its own copy under
%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Orca\\daemon-host-profiles and is never stopped. The switch runs
in a detached worker process, so it keeps going when the calling terminal or
client goes away.

Only official stablyai/orca GitHub releases are accepted. Installers are
verified against the sha256 digest GitHub publishes for each asset, their
Authenticode signature (SignPath Foundation) and their product version before
anything runs.

State lives in ~/.local/state/orca-desktop-update, outside AppData: the Microsoft
Store Python redirects its own new files under AppData into a private folder.
"""

